Time is `O(log n)` for insertion, key changes, and extraction. The simple access methods are `O(1)`. The internal list takes `O(n)` space. Important edge cases are an empty heap and extracting the last remaining value.

Kept the heap in a zero-based vector. The parent of `i` is `(i - 1) / 2`, so insertion moves the new value upward. After changing a value, it may need to move either up or down, so both checks are made.

For a quick dry run, inserting `7, 3, 5` gives `[3, 7, 5]`, then `[3, 7, 5]` after `5`. Changing index `1` to `1` moves it to the root.

